# in.npt_trajectory -- Stage D-3 worker fragment: single-stage NPT
# production MD WITH trajectory dump output for OVITO animation, on a
# ~100-150 atom supercell (AlNi 128 atoms, Al3Ni5 144 atoms).
#
# NOT standalone-runnable -- same reason as Stage D/D-2's fragments:
# pair_style mliap unified EXISTS requires the Python-side
# lammps.mliap.load_unified_kokkos() call before this file is read
# (confirmed empirically, see in.nvt_stability's header for the exact
# error). Load via lmp.file() from lammps_stage_d3_trajectory_run_phase.py
# AFTER read_data/model-load/pair setup on the SUPERCELL.
#
# dump fields are `id element xu yu zu`: "element" (not numeric type,
# resolved via dump_modify's element mapping below) and xu/yu/zu are
# LAMMPS-computed UNWRAPPED coordinates -- both explicitly requested, so
# atoms don't "teleport" across the periodic boundary between animated
# frames, and the dump file has real chemical symbols rather than numeric
# type codes needing a separate lookup table. Native LAMMPS dump text
# format is one of OVITO's most robust/native importers.
#
# Driver must set these LAMMPS variables before lmp.file()'ing this script:
#   temp          target temperature, K
#   seed          velocity-seed RNG integer
#   tdamp         Nose-Hoover thermostat damping time, ps
#   pdamp         barostat damping time, ps
#   pressure      target external pressure, bar (0.0 = ambient)
#   npt_steps     number of 1-fs steps to run
#   thermo_every  thermo/log sampling interval, steps
#   dump_every    trajectory dump interval, steps
#   dump_file     path to write the LAMMPS custom dump trajectory
#   final_data    path to write the post-NPT LAMMPS data file (provenance)
#
# Element order (fixed project-wide, ELEMENT_ORDER=["Al","Ni"], set by the
# driver's pair_coeff before this file runs): type 1 = Al, type 2 = Ni --
# dump_modify's element mapping below reuses this directly.

timestep 0.001

velocity all create ${temp} ${seed} mom yes rot yes dist gaussian

thermo ${thermo_every}
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz lx ly lz xy xz yz vol
thermo_modify flush yes

dump traj all custom ${dump_every} ${dump_file} id element xu yu zu
dump_modify traj element Al Ni sort id

print "=== STAGE D-3 NPT TRAJECTORY START ==="
fix mdintegrate all npt temp ${temp} ${temp} ${tdamp} tri ${pressure} ${pressure} ${pdamp}
run ${npt_steps}
print "=== STAGE D-3 NPT TRAJECTORY END ==="
unfix mdintegrate
undump traj

write_data ${final_data} nocoeff
